invariant: INV-33
file: webpki_cert.c
catches: webpki_auth_test
reason: under pins alone the key reader holds the leaf to the walk's
  CH_WEBPKI_CERT_MAX of 3072 bytes, though a Certificate message carries
  a leaf up to CH_WEBPKI_LEAF_PIN_CERT_MAX and the reader reads it only
  as far as its key. The QUIC Interop Runner's amplificationlimit leaf,
  5,514 bytes under a pinned key, fails with bad_certificate.
  test/webpki_leaf_pins.h's leaf_over_cert_max rows, which want the
  corpus leaf of 5,558 bytes accepted, object.

--- old
    if (!read_certificate_head(cert, cert_len, CH_WEBPKI_LEAF_PIN_CERT_MAX, &r, out)) {
--- new
    if (!read_certificate_head(cert, cert_len, CH_WEBPKI_CERT_MAX, &r, out)) {
